From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 12:56:22 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2177/2179] PCI: allow D3 for hotplug-capable root ports on
 Qualcomm PCIe

7.2.8 never lets a natively hotplug-capable root port into D3. The
Snapdragon X1 root ports report hotplug, so they stay in D0 through
system suspend, pci_host_common_d3cold_possible() fails, pcie-qcom keeps
a 1 kBps PCIe-to-DDR vote, and the SoC never reaches DDR sleep or CX
collapse.

Mainline 7.3 allows D3 for these ports on every non-x86 platform
(d4c79b63d82d, "PCI: Allow D3 for native hotplug-capable Root Ports on
non-x86 platforms", Manivannan Sadhasivam). This package also serves
ACPI arm64 machines whose root ports were never runtime-suspended on
7.2.8, so this backport limits the change to root ports on Qualcomm
PCIe controllers. Drop it when moving to 7.3.

On a Surface Pro 11 (X1E80100) in deep suspend: CX, AOSS and DDR asleep
99.9% of a one-hour suspend, about 0.23 W, instead of never.

Link: https://patch.msgid.link/20260729165005.896725-1-manivannan.sadhasivam@oss.qualcomm.com
Signed-off-by: Brandon Williams <turbine.bmw@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
---
 drivers/pci/pci.c | 17 +++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/pci/pci.c b/drivers/pci/pci.c
index 350bae907ebf..d9a85df81aec 100644
--- a/drivers/pci/pci.c
+++ b/drivers/pci/pci.c
@@ -2974,6 +2974,18 @@ static const struct dmi_system_id bridge_d3_blacklist[] = {
 	{ }
 };
 
+/*
+ * Root ports on Qualcomm (Snapdragon) PCIe controllers. Mainline allows D3
+ * for every non-x86 hotplug-capable root port from 7.3 (d4c79b63d82d); this
+ * 7.2.8 backport limits it to these so other arm64 hosts keep 7.2.8 behaviour.
+ */
+static bool pci_bridge_on_qcom_pcie(struct pci_dev *bridge)
+{
+	struct device *ctrl = pci_find_host_bridge(bridge->bus)->dev.parent;
+
+	return ctrl && ctrl->driver && !strcmp(ctrl->driver->name, "qcom-pcie");
+}
+
 /**
  * pci_bridge_d3_possible - Is it possible to put the bridge into D3
  * @bridge: Bridge to check
@@ -3022,9 +3034,10 @@ bool pci_bridge_d3_possible(struct pci_dev *bridge)
 		/*
 		 * Hotplug ports handled natively by the OS were not validated
 		 * by vendors for runtime D3 at least until 2018 because there
-		 * was no OS support.
+		 * was no OS support. Qualcomm's root ports report hotplug, and
+		 * keeping them in D0 keeps a DDR vote through system suspend.
 		 */
-		if (bridge->is_pciehp)
+		if (bridge->is_pciehp && !pci_bridge_on_qcom_pcie(bridge))
 			return false;
 
 		if (dmi_check_system(bridge_d3_blacklist))
-- 
2.56.0

